Input: arr[] = [1, 2, 4, 2], s = 1, x = 7
Output: true
Explanation: The first student gets 1 on paper and writes 2. The second student gets [1, 2] and writes 5. 
The third student gets [1, 2, 5] and writes 12. The final sequence of numbers on the paper is 1, 2, 5, 12, 22. Using 2 and 5 we can form 7. 
-------------------------

class Solution {
    public boolean isPossible(int[] arr, int s, int x) {
        // code here
        if(x==0) return true;
        
        if(s>x) return false;
        ArrayList<Long>list = new ArrayList<>();
        list.add((long)s);
        long currsum= s;
        
        for(int i=0;i<arr.length;i++){
            long newsum=currsum+arr[i];
            if(newsum>x) break;
            list.add(newsum);
            currsum+=newsum;
        }
        
        long target=x;
        for(int i=list.size()-1;i>=0;i--){
            if(list.get(i)<=target){
                target-=list.get(i);
            }
        }
        return target==0? true: false;
    }
}
